No solution needs the coefficients proportional but the constants out of step: $ rac{p}{12} =  rac{3}{q} 
e  rac{5}{20} =  rac{1}{4}$. From $ rac{p}{12} =  rac{3}{q}$ we get $pq = 36$. The second part says $ rac{p}{12} 
e  rac{1}{4}$, i.e. $p 
e 3$. Both parts are needed: $p = 3$ with $q = 12$ gives $3x + 3y = 5$ and $12x + 12y = 20$, which are the same line and have infinitely many solutions.
